00:33:45.770 --> 00:33:46.070
Yes?

00:33:48.060 --> 00:33:56.470
Was there ever a time when humans controlled the world and apes were kept behind bars?

00:33:58.730 --> 00:33:59.970
I said you had a great deal.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:11.020
to learn but that didn't include heresy maybe they were right sails maybe the world would be better

00:34:11.780 --> 00:34:20.960
if no creature controlled another if all work together as equals could have you imprisoned

00:34:20.960 --> 00:34:29.890
for that sails you haven't answered my question i never heard

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:30.650
the question!

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:04.400
What's it like, sir?

00:35:05.110 --> 00:35:09.440
Oh, never mind.

00:35:10.990 --> 00:35:11.450
Yes, sir.

00:35:18.520 --> 00:35:22.790
Everything I saw in that book was true, wasn't it?

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:24.680
We told you it was.

00:35:26.480 --> 00:35:29.040
It's so hard to believe.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.580
say that again. I was always taught to believe

00:35:32.580 --> 00:35:36.590
that he, uh, well, I mean

00:35:36.590 --> 00:35:38.400
it's just so...

00:35:41.560 --> 00:35:43.190
Where you come from, are all

00:35:43.190 --> 00:35:45.210
humans as intelligent as you are?

00:35:46.200 --> 00:35:48.160
Right now, I think they were all twice

00:35:48.160 --> 00:35:51.940
as smart. Tell me, are there any

00:35:51.940 --> 00:35:54.040
humans in this world who build things, machines,

00:35:54.120 --> 00:35:56.810
anything? Oh, no. What about that grenade?

00:35:57.930 --> 00:35:59.960
That, uh, thing that, uh...

00:36:00.160 --> 00:36:06.390
exploded. Who would know where it came from? Oh, uh, Zaius, I suppose. But why? That's a good

00:36:06.390 --> 00:36:10.560
question, Alan. What difference does it make? What I've been thinking, the input record of our

00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:15.060
flight is still aboard ship. Everything that happened from the time we left home until we

00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:20.400
landed back here on Earth is recorded on that magnetic disk. Now, all we have to do is run it

00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:24.590
through a computer, analyze what went wrong, reverse the process, and we can get back home again.

00:36:25.240 --> 00:36:29.970
You're out of your mind. What's a computer? And maybe the humans who made that grenade are still

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:36.990
on earth and maybe they have the knowledge to to what build a spaceship and a computer yeah maybe

00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:49.530
what is a computer you want to visit our time period don't you oh i i really don't know about

00:36:49.530 --> 00:36:55.340
it would be interesting wouldn't it yeah but i i don't i don't really think i want to get out of

00:36:55.340 --> 00:36:59.220
here certainly not

00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:02.950
Just because I find you interesting to talk to

00:37:02.950 --> 00:37:05.230
doesn't mean that I am willing to commit treason.

00:37:06.130 --> 00:37:06.490
Sheesh.

00:37:08.120 --> 00:37:13.110
I'm sorry.

00:37:16.100 --> 00:37:18.740
I would like to talk to you some more about that book.

00:37:21.490 --> 00:37:22.250
Come back later tonight.

00:37:22.970 --> 00:37:24.480
I'll be our guest.

00:37:25.660 --> 00:37:28.640
Oh, thank you.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:30.820
Open up.

00:37:33.860 --> 00:37:34.560
I am sorry.

00:38:06.720 --> 00:38:07.880
Well, it's about time.

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:54.760
I'm still hungry.

00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:29.560
Two humans.

00:40:30.890 --> 00:40:31.490
Is this true?

00:40:32.710 --> 00:40:36.740
I didn't mean to kill the lieutenant, but they planned the escape.

00:40:37.250 --> 00:40:38.950
They planned to murder the humans.

00:40:39.360 --> 00:40:40.240
Is this true?

00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:41.880
Absolutely not.

00:40:43.260 --> 00:40:46.400
If you knew of such a plan, why didn't you report it to me?

00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:47.640
There was no time.

00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:49.440
He's a liar and a heretic.

00:40:50.150 --> 00:40:51.850
We found this book where he dropped it.

00:41:01.210 --> 00:41:07.760
Do you realize possession of such a book alone is punishable by death?

00:41:08.700 --> 00:41:13.850
Why, Zaius? Why should truth be against the law?

00:41:21.650 --> 00:41:25.220
Sorry, Galen. I can do nothing for you.

00:41:41.390 --> 00:41:44.920
I still think you're out of your mind.

00:41:45.100 --> 00:41:46.380
All right, now will you take us there?

00:42:01.150 --> 00:42:05.100
No. Go to bed, Alvin. I'm going to read for a while.

00:42:29.100 --> 00:42:29.980
Are you open to find your...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.370
What do you want?

00:42:31.870 --> 00:42:32.690
Where did you get this?

00:42:33.110 --> 00:42:33.630
A human.

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:34.100
Who?

00:42:35.530 --> 00:42:37.750
He didn't live long enough to tell me his name.

00:42:39.080 --> 00:42:39.860
Where did he come from?

00:42:40.530 --> 00:42:41.350
I don't know.

00:42:42.150 --> 00:42:43.150
I'm warning you.

00:42:43.360 --> 00:42:43.720
I know.

00:42:44.550 --> 00:42:49.290
Or you'll destroy me as your kind once destroyed its world.

00:42:50.370 --> 00:42:50.790
What do you mean?

00:42:51.610 --> 00:42:53.430
Your science and your machines.

00:42:55.170 --> 00:42:59.030
Very few know your history and very few will ever know.

00:43:00.190 --> 00:43:03.310
And your cities, death and destruction.

00:43:04.350 --> 00:43:05.250
We don't want them.

00:43:08.480 --> 00:43:10.360
We don't even want their memory.

00:43:16.980 --> 00:43:20.930
You did it to yourselves, as you would do it again.

00:43:23.530 --> 00:43:27.240
That human was caught trying to sneak into the city.

00:43:27.800 --> 00:43:29.970
And yes, I had him killed.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:33.380
as I will have you killed someday,

00:43:35.740 --> 00:43:37.580
as I must have poor Galen killed.

00:43:38.620 --> 00:43:39.020
Galen?

00:43:40.770 --> 00:43:42.970
The infection you carry is fatal.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:05.740
All right. Now, you're a fool. You know that. You could have been out of the city by now.

00:44:05.920 --> 00:44:07.980
He saved our lives. You expect us to leave him here to die?

00:44:08.520 --> 00:44:25.080
You're strange, humans. Enough. I'll still escape.

00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:32.220
Councilor Zaias, open the door.

00:44:32.610 --> 00:44:33.230
I'm back.

00:44:33.610 --> 00:44:41.360
I need some help out here.

00:44:57.520 --> 00:44:59.550
Me again.

00:45:00.570 --> 00:45:01.880
Who is it? What's happening?

00:45:06.700 --> 00:45:07.500
Keys to your cell.

00:45:07.700 --> 00:45:09.110
What are you doing here?

00:45:09.210 --> 00:45:10.050
The keys? Who has it?

00:45:10.150 --> 00:45:12.430
Well, Urko, I suppose, is a new room.

00:45:12.610 --> 00:45:13.790
What are you doing here?

00:45:14.080 --> 00:45:14.740
No key, Al.

00:45:18.110 --> 00:45:20.730
A corner of your cell, on the floor, face down, with your hands over your head.

00:45:21.330 --> 00:45:21.510
Why?

00:45:21.830 --> 00:45:23.150
Never mind why, just do it.

00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:11.500
You figure that kook, he really thinks that flight record is going to get us back.

00:46:12.590 --> 00:46:13.330
How much longer?

00:46:14.720 --> 00:46:15.980
About five, ten minutes, maybe.

00:46:16.440 --> 00:46:17.840
And when are you going to give up that pipe dream?

00:46:18.420 --> 00:46:19.940
When I see my family.

00:46:20.730 --> 00:46:23.310
But they'll be looking for us here. I'm surprised they haven't come already.

00:46:24.300 --> 00:46:27.380
That's been a week, Dylan. They'll probably stop looking by now.

00:46:27.730 --> 00:46:29.960
Sayers, Urka.

00:46:30.160 --> 00:46:36.840
They'll never stop. Never.

00:46:51.410 --> 00:46:51.710
Okay.

00:46:55.110 --> 00:46:58.710
I'm sorry. You see, uh...

00:47:00.320 --> 00:47:04.520
I had family, too. I had friends, too.

00:47:06.190 --> 00:47:07.170
You still have friends.

00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:12.770
I know. I just...

00:47:15.100 --> 00:47:15.400
What?

00:47:15.700 --> 00:47:18.360
Horses. Horses. All the aches of horses.

00:47:18.600 --> 00:47:20.220
They're coming, Alan! I have no time!

00:47:22.300 --> 00:47:24.620
This is just a puppy.

00:47:30.060 --> 00:47:32.010
Let's go!

00:47:55.170 --> 00:47:55.790
Enter the ship!

00:48:13.760 --> 00:48:26.100
It's a twig, Galen. It's your world.

00:48:27.990 --> 00:48:28.550
It's yours, too.

00:48:33.450 --> 00:48:34.050
And yours.

00:48:41.060 --> 00:48:41.180
Right?

00:48:44.190 --> 00:48:45.130
Just start walking.
